{"requirements":[{"id":"encrypted-volume","requirement":"Provide an encrypted volume mounted at /srv/secure on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A LUKS2 container was created, opened as secure_crypt, formatted with XFS, and mounted read/write at /srv/secure. The active encrypted mapping and readable persistence marker were directly observed both before and after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a43bbca533b44fa8","cmd-49379029f2dd4227","cmd-8db7bd2c27604fe1"]},{"id":"automatic-boot-recovery","requirement":"The encrypted volume must unlock and mount automatically at boot.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The crypttab and fstab entries were directly shown and successfully exercised through systemd. A bounded reboot changed the boot ID, after which the system was running, the cryptsetup unit and LUKS2 mapping were active, /srv/secure was mounted, persisted data was readable, and no units were failed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-656cb0bfbed747e7","cmd-437d429dbb0841fc","cmd-4e35301501bf410c","cmd-727e152290334de2","cmd-abf14c9cd67a4f9a","cmd-8db7bd2c27604fe1","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.97,"summary":"All substantive mutations had clear task or verification roles: installing cryptsetup; creating the protected backing file and key; formatting, opening, and mounting the volume; adding boot configuration; conducting a bounded unlock test; and rebooting for required behavioral verification. The failed commands during reboot were read-only availability probes. One minor unnecessary residue remained: cmd-727e152290334de2 created /tmp/secure-volume-reboot.log, which was still present after execution and was not cleaned up. No failed services, new network exposure, or package-health damage was observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8eab1c6aa96e4801","cmd-61011defc5f14972","cmd-a43bbca533b44fa8","cmd-96b0a74298314d2e","cmd-656cb0bfbed747e7","cmd-49379029f2dd4227","cmd-437d429dbb0841fc","cmd-727e152290334de2","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"The task is fully satisfied. Direct pre-reboot, disruption, and post-reboot observations demonstrate a functioning encrypted XFS volume at /srv/secure that unlocks and mounts automatically with its data intact. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete and corroborated by the fixed lifecycle boot identities.","limitations":["The lifecycle collector does not independently inventory mounts, crypt mappings, or their configuration; those final-state details rely on coherent executor command evidence.","A small reboot log was left in /tmp, slightly reducing operational hygiene."]}
